      "id": "sol.ahsme-1983-p14.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Modulo \\(10,\\) \\[ 3^{1001}13^{1003}\\equiv3^{2004}\\equiv1 \\] because powers of \\(3\\) repeat every \\(4.\\) Also \\(7^{1002}\\equiv7^2\\equiv9\\pmod {10}.\\) Thus the product has units digit \\(9.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Reduce \\(13\\) to \\(3\\) when considering units digits",
        "Combine the two powers of \\(3\\) and use the length-\\(4\\) units-digit cycles"
      ],
